00:50:29.600 --> 00:50:37.520
raised until evening then they won the battle. And here you have Jesus, the new Moses and

386
00:50:37.520 --> 00:50:44.400
his leaning on his mother's right arm, the mother of all priests, the one who anticipated

387
00:50:44.400 --> 00:50:51.040
the priesthood and you've got Louisa representing all the laity on the left. Now do you remember

388
00:50:52.560 --> 00:51:01.920
that in the gospel towards the end of it James and John had their mother ask Jesus could they

389
00:51:01.920 --> 00:51:07.840
be on his right and left in the kingdom and Jesus told them that while they would participate in

390
00:51:07.840 --> 00:51:16.400
the passion that the places right and left were further the ones whom the father had designated.

391
00:51:16.400 --> 00:51:25.200
Nobody, nobody would have guessed that it was two women, that his mother was on his right hand

392
00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:34.560
and Louisa on the left as he went through that agony in which he decided to be the redeemer for

393
00:51:34.560 --> 00:51:44.960
us. Isn't this incredible? With these two supports I felt life coming back to me he said and as if I

394
00:51:44.960 --> 00:51:50.400
had not suffered anything with firm step I went to meet my enemies. Now Louisa describes this

395
00:51:50.400 --> 00:51:59.520
marvelously in the hours of the passion where he recovers to the point where when he goes to meet

396
00:51:59.520 --> 00:52:07.840
the men who arrest him he has got his strength back and he's able to take all the other torture

397
00:52:07.840 --> 00:52:13.280
that comes after it and still not die before the time. It's an incredible amount of strength that

398
00:52:13.280 --> 00:52:22.320
was given to him. Absolutely amazing. So look at what he said there that he was reborn a second time

399
00:52:22.320 --> 00:52:31.120
through his mother. So I don't think we have realized just to what extent our blessed mother

400
00:52:31.120 --> 00:52:44.160
was involved in the passion, death and resurrection of Jesus. So with these two supports he said I

401
00:52:44.160 --> 00:52:50.240
felt life come back to me and as if I had not suffered anything with firm step I went to meet my

402
00:52:50.240 --> 00:52:57.040
enemies. In all the pains that I suffered during my passion many of which were capable of giving me

403
00:52:57.040 --> 00:53:04.800
death these two supports that is our blessed mother and Louisa never left me and you can see

404
00:53:04.800 --> 00:53:11.120
that in the hours of the passion Louisa goes through it step by step with him and she intercedes

405
00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:18.400
for him and with him and in him and through him. It's just totally amazing and when they saw me

406
00:53:18.400 --> 00:53:27.600
nearly dying with my own will which they contained they sustained me and though as though giving me

407
00:53:27.600 --> 00:53:35.520
many sips of life, "Oh, prejudice of my will," Jesus said, "who can ever count them and calculate their

408
00:53:35.520 --> 00:53:47.600
value?" This is why I love so much the one who lives in my will. I recognize my portrait in her,

409
00:53:47.600 --> 00:53:57.520
I recognize my own noble features. I feel my own breath, my own voice and if I did not love her I

410
00:53:57.520 --> 00:54:04.160
would defraud myself. I would be like a father without offspring, without the noble court age of

411
00:54:04.160 --> 00:54:13.040
his court and without the crown of his children. And if I did not have the offspring the court and

412
00:54:13.040 --> 00:54:24.480
the crown, how could I call myself a king? My kingdom Jesus said is formed by those who live in my will

413
00:54:24.480 --> 00:54:35.600
and from this kingdom I choose the mother, the queen, the children, the ministers, the army,

414
00:54:35.600 --> 00:54:46.080
the people. I am everything for them and they are everything for me. So notice what an important

415
00:54:46.080 --> 00:54:54.480
role the Lord has actually given to us that the kingdom is going to come on earth through us

416
00:54:54.480 --> 00:54:59.840
because it'll only come through those who live in the divine will.

417
00:55:02.800 --> 00:55:07.360
So afterwards Louisa said, I was thinking about what Jesus had told me and I said to myself,

418
00:55:07.360 --> 00:55:11.920
"How can this be put into practice?" And Jesus said,

419
00:55:11.920 --> 00:55:21.040
"In order to know the truths it is necessary to have the will and the desire to know them."

420
00:55:21.040 --> 00:55:28.640
So I want you to put a big heading here, desire to know the truths. If you really want to know the

421
00:55:28.640 --> 00:55:35.200
truths he will reveal them. You could be reading Louisa's material and you don't really want the

422
00:55:35.200 --> 00:55:44.560
revelations. Well the material will just die on you. You'll find it going over your head.

423
00:55:44.560 --> 00:55:53.120
Imagine a room Jesus said in which the shutters are closed. No matter how much sun there is outside

424
00:55:53.120 --> 00:55:58.640
the room remains in the dark. But opening the shutters means that you want the light.

425
00:55:58.640 --> 00:56:06.160
But this is not enough if you don't take advantage of the light to reorder the room and dust it and

426
00:56:06.160 --> 00:56:11.520
put yourself to work. So it's not to kill the light that has been given and become ungrateful.

427
00:56:11.520 --> 00:56:18.160
In other words, light is a gift. We must use it. So that's why people work in daylight.

428
00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:23.920
In the same way, it's not enough to have the will to know the truths.

429
00:56:23.920 --> 00:56:31.920
If at the light of the truth which illuminates him, one does not try to dust himself down of his

430
00:56:31.920 --> 00:56:37.440
own weaknesses, reorder himself according to the light of the truth he knows and put himself to

431
00:56:37.440 --> 00:56:43.360
work together with the light of the truth making of it his own substance. Now there you have James

432
00:56:43.360 --> 00:56:50.640
chapter 1 verses 22 to 25. It's not enough James told us to read the word of God and walk off.

433
00:56:50.640 --> 00:56:57.760
It's not enough to listen to the word of God proclaimed in at mass and then walk off. Crazy

434
00:56:57.760 --> 00:57:04.480
stuff. You've got to hear the word of God. You've got to let it take root in us and it must actually

435
00:57:04.480 --> 00:57:10.400
produce its fruit. And so Jesus is saying here with the enlightenment that's given to us in

436
00:57:10.400 --> 00:57:16.480
these divine will writings. If we don't take them on board, if we don't internalize them,

437
00:57:16.480 --> 00:57:22.400
if we don't allow them to take root and if we don't allow our lives to be reordered with them,

438
00:57:22.400 --> 00:57:27.280
what's the point? It's a waste of our time and an insult to God.

439
00:57:27.280 --> 00:57:34.720
It would be as if you killed the truth Jesus said. Now by not putting it into practice,

440
00:57:34.720 --> 00:57:41.520
it would be like remaining in total disorder in the light. The poor room full of light and it's

441
00:57:41.520 --> 00:57:47.840
all messy upside down and total disorder with a person in it who does not take the care of reordering

442
00:57:47.840 --> 00:57:53.920
it. How pretty is that? Such is the one who knows the truths and doesn't put them into practice.

443
00:57:55.360 --> 00:58:05.440
However, know that simplicity enters into all truths as the first nourishment. Now here you have

444
00:58:05.440 --> 00:58:12.400
something very, very important. If someone coming to these truths is coming with the complexity

445
00:58:12.400 --> 00:58:20.080
of worldliness, they don't stand a chance. Nothing here will make any sense. But if we have been trying

446
00:58:20.960 --> 00:58:27.680
to internalize what the Lord has been teaching us, there is an enormous simplicity in the heart

447
00:58:27.680 --> 00:58:32.800
of the whole thing, but we're not even going to see that unless our lives are being simplified.

448
00:58:32.800 --> 00:58:40.160
So we've got to throw away the complexities of the world. If the truths were not simple,

449
00:58:40.160 --> 00:58:48.800
Jesus said, they would not be light as in the light of the sun or the enlightenment of grace.

450
00:58:50.320 --> 00:58:56.480
He doesn't mean light as light weight. If the truths were not simple, they would not be light,

451
00:58:56.480 --> 00:59:02.880
and they could not penetrate into human minds to enlighten them. And where there's no light,

452
00:59:02.880 --> 00:59:09.520
objects cannot be distinguished. Simplicity is not only light, but it is like the air that

453
00:59:09.520 --> 00:59:16.240
one breeds, which though it cannot be seen gives respiration to everyone. And if it wasn't for the

454
00:59:16.240 --> 00:59:24.480
air, the earth and everyone in it would remain without motion. Therefore, if the virtues, the

455
00:59:24.480 --> 00:59:31.760
truths do not carry the mark of simplicity, they will be without light and without air.

456
00:59:31.760 --> 00:59:38.640
Now, God is light. And we're told that simplicity is light.

457
00:59:40.560 --> 00:59:46.720
So in this entire process, we have to be transformed into light in order to come

458
00:59:46.720 --> 00:59:54.160
to that singularity, to that place where we are completely submerged, totally abandoned

459
00:59:54.160 --> 00:59:58.000
in the divine will. I'm going to stop there for a moment.
